27	 * tests create owners and read fields back via {@code GET /api/owners/{id}}, so the
28	 * Spring and OfficeFloor arms are judged by identical externals.
29	 *
30	 * <p>Isolation: {@code @Transactional} rolls each test back, so count/quota rules
31	 * (membership number, per-day cap, per-city cap, "most common city") see only the
32	 * seed data plus what the test itself creates — deterministic without polluting
33	 * other tests. {@code @WithMockUser} authenticates as a fixed admin so the audit
34	 * rules can assert a known user name.
35	 *
36	 * <p>Cumulative-safety convention: {@link #ownerNode()} returns a FULLY UNIQUE
37	 * owner, which every rule accepts (no duplicate, no quota) at every checkpoint;
38	 * tests then override only the fields needed to trigger a specific rule. Reject
39	 * cases use data that stays rejected under all later (broader) rules.
40	 */
41	@SpringBootTest
42	@AutoConfigureMockMvc
43	@Transactional
44	@WithMockUser(username = "acceptance-admin", roles = {"OWNER_ADMIN", "VET_ADMIN", "ADMIN"})
